pip freeze > requirements.txt: This takes a snapshot of your exact current environment and writes every library (and its exact version) into requirements.txt. Later, when we deploy this to a Docker container, Docker will just read this file and instantly replicate your environment.

pydantic: like typescript, we define a type of data or object and only that particular type is allowed, all other data would be restrcited from entering.

We can share data in 3 ways in FastAPI:
    -> path parameter: part of URL (To identify a specific resource)
        eg: Example: GET /problems/42 -> 42 is path parameter (bring Problem ID 42).
    -> query parameter: Sent @ end of url using "?" Majorly for filtering or Sorting
        eg: Example: GET /problems?difficulty=hard -> Query parameter here is "hard"
    -> req body: When data is Large || Insensitive, we don't see it in the url, but in the req body

FastAPI = a main "Process" of backend and If we run our C++ || Other lang code in this, if code crash/lags --> whole BACKEND CRASHES :. we create "CHILD PROCESS" to avoid this;
    -> use "SubProcess Library for the same"